# device-layer-0010.
# The network: whether the device is online and how, through NWPathMonitor on macOS and iOS, ConnectivityManager
# on Android, the network interfaces on a desktop JVM, and navigator.onLine in a browser.
#
#   network-status   `<online|offline> <kind>`, the kind wifi, cellular, wired, other or none
#
# A host with no such capability (the server, the memory host) answers `unavailable`. Every answer is text from the
# closed set above, so an app compares strings and no platform enum ever reaches it.

load ./native/{platform}/network
  find read-network
  find follow-network

task network-status
  like text
  send back
    call read-network

# the answer above now and at every change the platform reports, to `handler`, until the task it answers is called.
# Any number at once, each dropped by its own task, and one subscription to the platform between them, ended by
# the last drop. A watcher started while others run hears the current answer at once
task watch-network
  take handler
    like task
      take value, like text
  like task
  send back
    call follow-network
      read handler
